From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A CI <ci@vyos-ls1046a>
Date: Thu, 17 Jul 2026 19:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_pcd: fix FE_ENTER compose target (EXT_HASH, not ENQ)

The 0158 compose function __fman_pcd_fe_build_vm_chain() used the first
ENQ FE's MURAM offset as the FE_ENTER target.  This is architecturally
wrong: FE_ENTER dispatches to the chain head (the EXT_HASH FE), not the
terminal disposition (the ENQ FE).  The EXT_HASH FE performs the hardware
hash lookup and routes HIT→MUX→ENQ or MISS→EXIT — it is the first FE
that frames encounter after FE_ENTER, not ENQ.

With the ENQ offset as target, frames entering the FE-VM bypass the ehash
lookup entirely, going straight to the ENQ disposition (FQ 0x200).  No
flow matching occurs regardless of inserted keys.

Fix: use pcd->fe_hash_off (set by fe_hash_build() above) as the FE_ENTER
target.  The EXT_HASH FE must have been built immediately before this
call (fe_hash_build returns error before we reach here if it wasn't).

Reference: arch/fman-microcode-210-programming-reference.md §2 and §7.2.
The EXT_HASH FE byte layout defines word5=nextFEPtr (HIT→MUX) and
word6=missNextFE (MISS→EXIT).  The FE_ENTER's word3 is the chain head.

Signed-off-by: VyOS LS1046A CI <ci@vyos-ls1046a>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
@@ -2403,14 +2403,14 @@ static int __fman_pcd_fe_build_vm_chain(struct fman_pcd *pcd)
 	 * FE_ENTER root AD links the classifier to the FE chain.
-	 * Use the first ENQ FE's MURAM offset as the chain head.
-	 * TODO: store enq_off for future flow_add() use.
+	 * Dispatch to the EXT_HASH FE (not ENQ) — the EXT_HASH FE
+	 * performs the hardware hash lookup and routes HIT→MUX→ENQ
+	 * or MISS→EXIT (§7.2).  The ENQ FE is the terminal
+	 * disposition, not the chain head.
 	 */
 	{
-		struct fman_pcd_fe_obj *e;
-
-		if (list_empty(&pcd->fe_enq))
-			return -ENOENT;
-
-		e = list_first_entry(&pcd->fe_enq,
-				     struct fman_pcd_fe_obj, node);
-		err = fman_pcd_fe_enter_build(pcd, e->muram_off);
+		err = fman_pcd_fe_enter_build(pcd, pcd->fe_hash_off);
 		if (err)
 			return err;
 	}
